		},
		{
			"id":"295da5d419d990b3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"MySleep()",
			"styleAttributes":{
				"textAlign":null
			},
			"x":-340,
			"y":1180,
			"width":360,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"72bc0e13540b90fd",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Flow of execution\n\n1. main calls readShellcode to read the shellcode from a file\n2. injectShellcode allocates memory and puts the shellcode into the it, and sets the appropriate permissions\n3. executeShellcode executes the shellcode from memory. This shellcode relies on windows api functions, which are hooked in the current process.\n4. The hooked windows API function executes, where a trampoline was inserted, and it jumps to our subroutine \"MySleep\"\n5. In MySleep, the return address is modified, because we trampolined from the DLL, so we need to find our way back.",
			"styleAttributes":{
				"textAlign":null
			},
			"x":100,
			"y":830,
			"width":660,
			"height":350
		},
		{
			"id":"d15ade30fb0c9d72",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Exported DLL Function",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-340,
			"y":800,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		}
	],
